macOS Hammerspoon driver performance, measured off-Mac. Pure-Lua costs of the macOS driver (static/ergopti_plus/macos) reproduce on Linux under the stubbed Hammerspoon test harness (lua5.4; also try luajit where the code is 5.1-compatible, but Hammerspoon runs Lua 5.4, so lua5.4 numbers are the reference). Read .agents/skills/perf-profiling/SKILL.md, .agents/skills/hammerspoon-driver/SKILL.md, docs/memory/macos-hammerspoon.md and docs/memory/rejected_proposals.md first. The handover (top of docs/ERGOPTIPLUS_TODO.md, "Performance state per OS", macOS line) lists the field numbers to explain: menu rebuild 113-247 ms, boot stages, preview 21-29 ms per key, preferences writes of 300 operations, ingest tick 1.0-1.5 s, and the phase counters in `infra/phase_stats.lua` (447da88d). Build a micro-benchmark harness (reuse macos/tests/bench if present, and the stubs) with realistic fixture data (the shipped hotstring packs, a full config.toml, a keystats journal of realistic size), measure each of those paths (median of >= 5 runs, os.clock and wall), find the CPU-bound Lua hot spots (a sampling hook via debug.sethook or a simple instrumented profiler), and optimise the dominant ones, one lever per commit with before/after numbers and a regression guard. Costs that are native (AX calls, hs.task, canvas drawing, Karabiner) cannot be measured here: list them as needing the Mac's `Phase summary` lines instead of guessing. Write docs/audits/performance/2026-10-24-macos-lua-profile.md with the numbers and reproduction commands. Run the full macOS stubbed suite before each push.
